\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: \uc2 Ford\uc2  Delays Office Return to January\b0\par\par\uc2 By Nora Naughton \par \uc2 286 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 August 2021\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ford Motor Co\uc2  . will not send employees back to the office until early next year due to the continued spread of the Covid-19 Delta variant, the company told employees Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The Dearborn, Mich.-based auto maker is telling employees globally who are able to do their jobs remotely to continue working from home until January, pushing back the company's return-to-work plans by three months.\par \par \uc2 "We will continue monitoring the virus and as conditions improve, explore opportunities for team members to return on-site for collaboration and teamwork," \uc2 Ford\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Ford\uc2  had planned to reopen offices in October with a new hybrid work model for those coming back to the workplace.\par \par \uc2 The company last year began reconfiguring its office spaces to accommodate a new era in which workers will have more freedom to do their jobs remotely. \uc2 Ford\uc2  still plans to implement the hybrid model when employees can safely return, a \uc2 Ford\uc2  spokesman said.\par \par \uc2 Ford\uc2  has about 182,000 employees worldwide. About half of them are salaried workers.\par \par \uc2 The office reopening plans apply to those working in jobs that are not dependent on being on site.\par \par \uc2 In \uc2 Ford\uc2  's U.S. factories, assembly line workers have continued to work throughout much of the pandemic under new safety protocols implemented to guard against the virus's spread.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, \uc2 Ford\uc2  , along with rivals \uc2 General Motors Co\uc2  . and \uc2 Jeep\uc2 -owner \uc2 Stellantis NV\uc2  reinstated mask mandates for workers at all factories, offices and warehouses, regardless of vaccination status.\par \par \uc2 The car companies cited new federal guidelines and the recent rise in infections from the Delta variant as prompting them to make the move.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020210826eh8q0000s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
