\par\par \uc2 World-Wide\par \uc2 What's News\par \b \uc2 World-Wide\b0\par\par\uc2 229 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 July 2021\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A significant uptick in Covid-19 cases across the U.S. is leading to new vaccination mandates for public employees, with the VA becoming the first federal agency, California the first state, and New York the first major city to announce requirements for their workers.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. won't lift restrictions on international travel at this point, a White House official said, citing rising coronavirus cases at home and abroad caused by the Delta variant.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 A push to complete a roughly $1 trillion infrastructure agreement hit a series of hurdles, as aides squabbled over funding for water infrastructure and other issues.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Biden said the U.S. combat mission in Iraq would conclude by the end of 2021, but the U.S. military would continue to work with Iraqi forces against Islamic State.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Civilian casualties of war in Afghanistan surged in the first half of the year as the U.S. began withdrawing its forces and the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  launched an offensive, a U.N . report said.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 U.S. and Chinese officials sparred over Covid-19, human rights and cybersecurity in the highest-level meetings between the two countries on Chinese soil since Biden became president.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Authorities said they identified the remains of the final victim of the condo collapse in Surfside, Fla., who hadn't been accounted for, bringing the death toll to 98.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020210727eh7r0001v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
