\par\par \b \uc2 EXCHANGE --- The Score: The Business Week in 7 Stocks\b0\par\par\uc2 By Francesca Fontana \par \uc2 694 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 June 2021\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ZOOM VIDEO COMMUNICATIONS INC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ZM -2.5%\par \par \uc2 The reopening of offices is not slowing Zoom's connection. Zoom's customer count rose and revenue nearly tripled in the first quarter, as the company expands beyond its initial focus to offer services such as webinars and chat. Zoom is trying to aid businesses that have some staff returning to offices while others continue to work remotely. These include Zoom Rooms, a take on the traditional conference room, and Zoom Phone, which the company sells as a telephone option for huddle rooms and executive offices. Zoom shares fell 2.5% Thursday.\par \par \uc2 TESLA INC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 TSLA -3%\par \par \uc2 Securities regulators are trying to cage \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 's tweets. The Wall Street Journal reported Tuesday that the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  told Tesla last year that its chief executive's use of \uc2 Twitter\uc2  had twice violated a court-ordered policy requiring his tweets to be preapproved by company lawyers. Tesla and the SEC settled an enforcement action in 2018 alleging that Mr. Musk had committed fraud by tweeting about a potential buyout of his company. Mr. Musk also publicly mocked the SEC even after settling fraud claims with the agency. Tesla shares fell 3% Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 ETSY INC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ETSY +7.2%\par \par \uc2 Etsy\uc2  is placing a large bid on the booming secondhand goods market. The online marketplace on Wednesday said it agreed to buy Depop for $1.63 billion. \uc2 Etsy\uc2  said the deal, consisting mainly of cash, gives the company access to the privately held marketplace's younger, fashion-conscious audience. London-based Depop, founded in 2011, has a community of roughly 30 million registered users across nearly 150 countries, with 4 million active buyers and 2 million active sellers in 2020. Many of its sellers begin by listing items from their own wardrobe. \uc2 Etsy\uc2  shares added 7.2% Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 PERSHING SQUARE TONTINE HOLDINGS LTD.\par \par \uc2 PSTH -12%\par \par \uc2 A hedge-fund billionaire has the ear of the world's largest music business. A special-purpose acquisition company controlled by \uc2 William Ackman\uc2  is nearing a deal with \uc2 Universal Music Group\uc2  that would give the SPAC a stake in \uc2 Universal\uc2  and value the business at about $40 billion. \uc2 Universal\uc2  is the record label behind artists including Lady Gaga, Taylor Swift and Billie Eilish. Its stable also includes classic acts such as the Beatles, and last year it bought Bob Dylan's entire publishing catalog. Pershing Square Tontine shares declined 12% Friday.\par \par \uc2 UNITED AIRLINES HOLDINGS INC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 UAL -4.3%\par \par \uc2 United is planning to fly faster than sound. The airline said on Thursday that it would acquire 15 supersonic planes being developed by \uc2 Boom Technology Inc\uc2 ., to cut travel times and appeal to higher-paying fliers. Boom hopes to fly a scaled-down prototype later this year or early in 2022, with the 88-seat version targeted to carry passengers by 2029. The deal would resurrect high-speed flights more than two decades after that method of travel was grounded because of high costs and concerns about noise. United shares lost 4.3% Thursday.\par \par \uc2 APPLE INC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 AAPL -1.2%\par \par \uc2 Apple\uc2  is slicing up its workweek. In an email to staff, Chief Executive \uc2 Tim Cook\uc2  told office employees that they are expected to return to their workspace three days a week starting in September. The iPhone maker said it wants most office workers to show up Mondays, Tuesdays and Thursdays, with the option to work remotely on Wednesdays and Fridays. All of \uc2 Apple\uc2 's U.S. retail outlets welcomed back shoppers in March, and Mr. Cook said all stores in other markets would open by the end of the month. \uc2 Apple\uc2  shares fell 1.2% Thursday.\par \par \uc2 AMC ENTERTAINMENT HOLDINGS INC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 AMC\uc2  +95%\par \par \uc2 Meme stocks are rocketing higher again. \uc2 AMC\uc2  surged this past week, cementing its status as the darling of investors who post rocket-ship emojis and calls to send stocks "to the moon." Shares of other stocks popular with small investors such as \uc2 GameStop Corp\uc2 . have also surged over the past two weeks, a rally reminiscent of the Reddit-fueled craze of late January. \uc2 AMC\uc2 's wild week included a 95% gain Wednesday.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw380\pich316\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal5700\pichgoal4740
