\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. News: Unions Say Mexico Auto-Parts Maker Violates Trade Deal\b0\par\par\uc2 By Yuka Hayashi \par \uc2 618 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 May 2021\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A7\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON -- U.S. and Mexican labor groups filed a complaint against a Mexican auto-parts manufacturer, alleging that it violated the U.S.-Mexico-Canada Agreement by suppressing its workers' rights to unionize.\par \par \uc2 The complaint, filed Monday with the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2 , is the first case that seeks to use a new labor-dispute provision of the USMCA trade agreement signed into law last year by former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  with bipartisan support.\par \par \uc2 The complaint provides an early test of President Biden's pledge to press for strict adherence to labor and environmental rules under existing trade agreements.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for the U.S. Trade Representative's office, which will be one of the agencies reviewing the complaint, said the agency would carefully review it. \uc2 Mexico's Economy Ministry\uc2  said it hadn't been notified of the complaint and had no comment.\par \par \uc2 The complaint from the labor groups led by \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  alleges that Tridonex, an auto-parts factory located in the Mexican state of Tamaulipas, "harassed and fired" workers who were trying to organize with a Mexican labor group seeking to improve wages and working conditions.\par \par \uc2 A lawyer representing the workers, Susana Prieto, was jailed for a month by local officials before agreeing to a ban on appearing in labor court, the complainants said.\par \par \uc2 Tridonex, a subsidiary of Philadelphia-based \uc2 Cardone Industries Inc\uc2 ., manufactures auto parts exported to the U.S. market.\par \par \uc2 A Cardone spokesman said the company doesn't believe the allegations in the complaint are accurate and would welcome a full inquiry. "We fully support our Tridonex workers being represented by a union and are committed to compliance with all applicable labor laws and regulations," he said.\par \par \uc2 AFL-CIO President \uc2 Richard Trumka\uc2  said the alleged harassment was a "textbook violation of the labor laws Mexico has pledged to uphold."\par \par \uc2 Other complainants were the \uc2 Service Employees International Union\uc2  (SEIU), \uc2 Public Citizen\uc2  and SNITIS -- the Sindicato Nacional Independiente de Trabajadores de Industrias y de Servicios Movimiento 20/32.\par \par \uc2 U.S. union leaders were among those pressing for tougher labor-enforcement provisions in the USMCA. They said that its predecessor agreement, the \uc2 North American Free Trade Agreement\uc2 , didn't have sufficient measures, leading to U.S. manufacturing job losses.\par \par \uc2 The USMCA's provision for labor-dispute settlement, known as the Rapid Response Labor Mechanism, makes it easier for labor unions to bring complaints against specific facilities in Mexico.\par \par \uc2 Still, the dispute, which could result in a punitive step against the company including the imposition of an import tariff by the U.S., could take months to unfold.\par \par \uc2 A committee made up of officials from the Trade Representative's office and the Commerce Department will first review the case. And if it determines a violation has occurred, the U.S. will then request the Mexican government to investigate the case and come up with a remedy.\par \par \uc2 If the dispute isn't resolved then, an international panel of experts will review under the provisions of USMCA.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Trade Representative Katherine Tai has said in recent weeks she was eager to take steps to enforce the rules of the USMCA.As a House congressional staffer for the Democrats, Ms. Tai played a significant role in designing and negotiating the USMCA, which replaced Nafta last year.\par \par \uc2 "My view is that we did our very best to put in the most effective tools for enforcement that we know how," Ms. Tai said during a Senate hearing last month. "I am not afraid to use the enforcement tools."\par \par \uc2 She noted that the U.S. has "a number of concerns" with Mexico's performance of its commitments under USMCA.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020210511eh5b0001g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
