\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: Google Lays Out Workplace Flexibility\b0\par\par\uc2 By Tripp Mickle \par \uc2 389 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 May 2021\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Alphabet Inc\uc2 .'s \uc2 Google\uc2  announced a series of moves to offer employees more workplace flexibility, allowing a fifth of its staff to work from home permanently and another fifth of workers to shift to a different geographic location.\par \par \uc2 In an email Wednesday, Alphabet Chief Executive \uc2 Sundar Pichai\uc2  said the company envisions that about 20% of staff would work from home on a permanent basis, while another 20% of staff would shift to new offices. The remaining 60% of staff will work from their current location. Employees will have to apply for both location-change options, with approval being up to their managers.\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2  is also moving to a hybrid workweek, where employees work from offices about three days a week, and two days "wherever they work best," Mr. Pichai said in the email.\par \par \uc2 The company also will offer four weeks per year where staff can work from anywhere with manager approval, a move that aims to give employees more flexibility around summer and holiday travel.\par \par \uc2 "The future of work is flexibility," Mr. Pichai said. He said the changes aimed to help staff do their best work.\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2  has been at the forefront of the move by tech companies to relax requirements that the workforce be in the office. \uc2 Salesforce Inc\uc2 ., \uc2 Microsoft Corp\uc2 . and others have adopted hybrid-work policies where staff will be able to work remotely during part of the week.\par \par \uc2 Facebook Inc. Chief Executive \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2  has said he expects as much as half of the company's workforce -- currently numbering more than 45,000 -- to work from home within 10 years.\par \par \uc2 The flexibility embraced by tech contrasts with major banks such as \uc2 Wells Fargo & Co\uc2 . and \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 , which expect most of their workforces to return to the office following the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 The closure of offices during the pandemic has forced major employers to re-evaluate the value of having people in the same physical space. With tools such as Zoom allowing people to continue to meet remotely, many companies are adopting a hybrid approach, noting that offices remain important to collaborating and preserving a workplace culture.\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2 , which has 140,000 employees, is headquartered in Mountain View, Calif., and the majority of its staff work in the Bay Area. However, it has offices in 19 states.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020210506eh560002u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
